This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge and road sign tests in Michigan. The issuing authority is the Michigan Department of State, led by the Secretary of State, and the source is the handbook What Every Driver Must Know. This section covers white and yellow pavement lines, crosswalk and stop lines, directional arrows, bicycle and shared lane markings, the left-turn-only center lane, Michigan Lefts, yield lines, traffic signal colors, the doghouse signal, flashing signals, the flashing yellow arrow left-turn signal, pedestrian signals and the Pedestrian Hybrid Beacon. The handbook pages do not state an official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the Secretary of State knowledge test, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them and records each as an explicit unknown. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy, never an official threshold.
